  <event id="228">
      <start>10:00</start>
      <duration>00:45</duration>
      <room>K.3.601</room>
      <slug></slug>
      <title>Systems Management with Matahari </title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>Configuration and Systems Management Devroom</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In this talk I will introduce the Matahari project, an interface for system management APIs of all kinds.&lt;/p&gt;      </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt; I will discuss the architecture of the Matahari ecosystem and how the use of AMQP as a transport layer allows it to scale to large collections of servers in the Cloud. I will also describe the ways in which developers and sysadmins can get involved in the Matahari ecosystem: by creating agents to provide access to existing APIs through Matahari; by creating their own APIs; by writing their own clients to interact with agents; and by interacting through a command line shell or script.&lt;/p&gt;      </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="2281">Zane Bitter</person>
      </persons>
